From 735c910683af668ce8b08c8b3720e660d870971c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:19:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(adaptive): bound the growth planner by the geometry it
 works, not only path length

The #13 budget counts revolution length, but the planner's time is
whole-ring polygon work per trial step: the island fixture ran ~53 s
(release) before the length budget refused it. A third budget law now
counts the polygon vertices every trial step and revolution runs
through (deterministic, never a wall clock); past 500 k the plan is
refused by name and the trochoid / Offset-ring fallback stays named.
Every fixture that grows today spends at most half of it (slot 252 k,
channel 175 k); the island is refused after 88 revolutions, 19 s
release / 39 s debug for the whole pocket.

Fixes #850

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
